{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then layer deterministic specifications that map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one recovery or exploration action. The policy favors move_forward in clear space, allows occasional random_walk only from clear/search context, uses directed turns for side obstacles, uses a brief backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path. Action states are one-shot in the specifications, with obstacle events able to preempt for safety while path_clear usually self-loops in commit states to respect open-loop pulse execution.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant sensing from motion capability so specifications can encode safe perception-to-action bindings cleanly",
    "Use forward as the dominant exploration action, with random_walk only as a secondary clear-space option",
    "Route obstacle_front through a dedicated backward recovery before a short directed turn",
    "Route obstacle_left to rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right to rotate_counterclockwise consistently",
    "Introduce a small stuck/last_resort chain so full_rotate is only reachable after repeated blocked conditions"
  ],
